From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] riched20: the OLE container side of the control, and pictures pasted as pictures (6002)

The rich edit control's IRichEditOle, client site and in-place site left most
of the OLE container work undone (RE-OLE): an embedded object could not be
saved by its site, activated in place, converted, or given host names, and a
picture pasted from Paint was refused.

IRichEditOle: SetHostNames (objects get them as they are inserted),
HandsOffStorage and SaveCompleted (the object lets go of its storage, takes
the new one), SetDvaspect (content or icon, re-laid out), SetLinkAvailable
(linked objects only), ConvertObject (the storage names the new class and
user type, the object is loaded again from it), ActivateAs (CoTreatAsClass,
and the objects of the class are loaded again), InPlaceDeactivate (the object
active in place), ImportDataObject (the data object or the clipboard replaces
the selection, in the given format or the best one). The client site's
SaveObject saves the object to its storage; GetMoniker (E_NOTIMPL: no links
to embedded objects), GetContainer (E_NOINTERFACE) and RequestNewObjectLayout
(E_NOTIMPL, not used) answer as documented. The in-place site:
CanInPlaceActivate (not for an icon), OnInPlaceActivate/Deactivate
(REO_INPLACEACTIVE), OnUIActivate/Deactivate (ShowContainerUI), GetWindowContext
(the host's GetInPlaceContext, the object's rectangle in the text), Scroll,
DiscardUndoState, DeactivateAndUndo, OnPosRectChange. Pasting CF_DIB or
CF_BITMAP inserts a picture object. Not done: the icon metafile of
ImportDataObject, OLE links (COM-OLELINK).
